---
import { site } from "../site";
---

<section class="section" aria-labelledby="founder-title">
  <div class="wrap">
    <article class="letter">
      <div class="photo" aria-hidden="true">
        <img src="/kunal.png" alt="" width="84" height="96" decoding="async" />
      </div>
      <span class="eyebrow">A note from the founder</span>
      <h2 id="founder-title">
        Hi, I'm Kunal.
        <br />
        <em>I'm building send0.</em>
      </h2>
      <div class="body">
        <p>
          I build software for a living, and more of it every month is agents. They keep hitting the same wall: email. A sign-up needs a
          code. A supplier answers a purchase order. A customer replies to a thread. The agent needs an inbox of its own, and there wasn't a
          good way to give it one.
        </p>
        <p>
          The hosted options were closed source, and some kept basics like webhooks for their priciest plans. Running your own mail server
          means weeks of DNS, deliverability and MIME before you write any agent code.
        </p>
        <p>So I'm building the inbox API I wanted, in the open. If you're giving agents email, write to me. I read every message.</p>
      </div>
      <footer class="sign">
        <div>
          <span class="name">Kunal Dholiya</span>
          <span class="role">Founder, send0</span>
        </div>
        <div class="links mono">
          <a href={site.founderGithub} rel="noopener">
            github.com/kunal-dd
          </a>
          <a href={`mailto:${site.email.hello}`}>{site.email.hello}</a>
        </div>
      </footer>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .letter {
    position: relative;
    max-width: 760px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 44px 28px 32px;
    background: var(--card);
    border: 1px solid var(--hairline);
    border-radius: 4px;
    box-shadow: var(--shadow);
  }
  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .letter {
      padding: 56px 64px 40px;
    }
  }
  /* Kunal, as the stamp in the corner */
  .photo {
    display: block;
    width: fit-content;
    margin: 0 0 18px;
    padding: 7px;
    background: var(--stamp-paper);
    transform: rotate(-3deg);
    filter: drop-shadow(0 4px 8px rgb(60 40 20 / 0.18));
    --r: 3.5px;
    mask:
      radial-gradient(var(--r) at var(--r) var(--r), #0000 97%, #000) calc(-1 * var(--r)) calc(-1 * var(--r)) / 11px 11px round,
      linear-gradient(#000 0 0) content-box;
  }
  .photo img {
    width: 64px;
    height: 74px;
    object-fit: cover;
    background: var(--sky);
  }
  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .photo {
      float: right;
      margin: -28px -32px 12px 24px;
      transform: rotate(3deg);
    }
    .photo img {
      width: 84px;
      height: 96px;
    }
  }
  h2 {
    font-size: clamp(28px, 3.2vw, 38px);
    line-height: 1.1;
  }
  h2 em {
    color: var(--postal-ink);
  }
  .body {
    margin-top: 22px;
  }
  .body p {
    font-size: 17px;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--ink) 82%, transparent);
  }
  .body p + p {
    margin-top: 14px;
  }
  .sign {
    clear: both;
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: flex-end;
    gap: 16px;
    margin-top: 30px;
    padding-top: 22px;
    border-top: 1.5px dashed var(--rule);
  }
  .name {
    display: block;
    font: italic 400 26px/1.1 var(--font-display);
  }
  .role {
    font-size: 13.5px;
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  .links {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 6px 18px;
    font-size: 12.5px;
  }
  .links a {
    color: var(--muted);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
    text-decoration-color: var(--rule);
  }
  .links a:hover {
    color: var(--ink);
  }
</style>
